# Loveable Azure Guardrails

## Preserve framework invariants

- Keep `.lovable/` files.
- Keep `vite.config.ts` on `@lovable.dev/vite-tanstack-config`.
- Keep TanStack Start file-based routing under `src/routes/`.
- Keep `src/start.ts`, `src/server.ts`, and Nitro `preset: "node-server"`.
- Treat `src/routeTree.gen.ts` as generated and never edit it manually.

## Keep responsibilities separated

- Put Azure hosting and deployment changes in `infra/` and `.github/workflows/`.
- Put schema changes in `supabase/migrations/`.
- Keep app code portable; avoid IIS, `web.config`, or Windows-hosting assumptions unless explicitly requested.

## Avoid breaking Loveable development

- Do not add duplicate Vite plugins already provided by Loveable.
- Do not migrate the app to Next.js, Remix, or another routing model.
- Do not swap core framework packages unless the task explicitly requires a migration.

## Check before large edits

- `.lovable/project.json`
- `vite.config.ts`
- `src/routes/README.md`
- `package.json`
- `infra/main.bicep`
- `supabase/config.toml`
